      }
    }
    return result;
  }

  return value;
}
```

## What changed

- **Object properties whose value is `undefined` are omitted** — the key is dropped entirely from the result. This check runs *after* normalization, so it also catches any value that normalizes to `undefined` (currently nothing does, but it keeps the rule future-proof).
- **Array `null` entries are preserved.** `Array.prototype.map` keeps every index, so `null` (whether original or produced from an empty string) stays in place. Arrays keep positional meaning; objects don't.

## Examples

```javascript
